<script>
 import {onMount} from 'svelte';
 import {BookOpen, Search, ArrowRight, Check, ChevronDown} from 'lucide-svelte';
 let {onnavigate=()=>{}}=$props();
 let query=$state(''); let completed=$state([]); let active=$state('start'); let ready=$state(false);
 const lessons=[
 {id:'start',title:'Find your way around',time:'2 min',page:'overview',action:'Explore the overview',intro:'Your project is the home for a story. Select it first so the workspace and libraries show the right world.',steps:['Choose a story in the project selector at the top of the sidebar. Projects shows all your story spaces and lets you open or create one.','Overview summarizes the selected story. Story workspace opens its scenes and canvas. Characters, Locations, and Themes & threads contain reusable story records.','Use the sidebar collapse button for more room. On mobile, open the navigation menu. Use the sun or moon in the top bar to change the theme.','Open Quick search or press Ctrl K to jump to a page or scene. Press Esc to close dialogs. The right inspector can be shown or hidden from the top bar.'],tip:'Tutorial progress saves on this browser. Exploring a lesson never changes your story.'},
 {id:'create',title:'Start a story your way',time:'3 min',page:'projects',action:'Open projects',intro:'Start with an empty world, a written story, or a complete PDF.',steps:['Open Projects and choose the new story action. Give the story a clear title and description.','Choose Manual Creation to build the cast, places, and scenes yourself. Story text and PDF intake can prepare editable draft records for review.','For a PDF, choose the PDF import option and select your document. Review Scenes, Characters, Locations, Themes, PDF images, Missing details, and Source pages before saving.','Correct the extracted names and descriptions. Assign each extracted image to its actual character, location, scene, or theme. Save the reviewed story to open its connected canvas.'],tip:'PDF extraction reads the document text and explicit clues. It is not semantic AI analysis. Scanned pages need OCR, which is not connected; unclear or missing details require review.'},
 {id:'assets',title:'Create or import your story world',time:'3 min',page:'characters',action:'Open characters',intro:'Keep a single reusable identity for every character and a distinct reference for every place.',steps:['Open Characters and choose Add character. Create/Generate starts a new profile; Import your own accepts an existing image or a supported JSON record.','Edit the name, description, appearance, personality, and clothing. A portrait can be imported now; it is not automatically a complete turnaround sheet.','For a generated reference, review the prompt for full-body front, back, side, three-quarter views, facial close-ups, and expressions. Inspect the result and approve the version you want to reuse.','Use Add location in Locations for each distinct environment. Use Add theme in Themes & threads for thematic descriptions or imported moodboards. Scene intake offers the same create/import choice.'],tip:'An imported image is assigned to the record you choose. A character reference establishes identity; a location reference establishes the setting; neither replaces a scene image.'},
 {id:'canvas',title:'Connect the storyboard canvas',time:'4 min',page:'scenes',action:'Open story workspace',intro:'Nodes represent reusable story elements. Connections carry information into a scene.',steps:['Open Story workspace and select the canvas view. Select a node to inspect its properties. Drag the card body to move it.','Connect a character or location output handle to a scene input handle. The scene then uses those connected references. A scene can include multiple characters.','Connect scene moments to establish narrative order or create another branch. Connect themes to scenes to describe where a thread appears.','Use Arrange, fit-to-view, and zoom controls to organize the graph. Use undo/redo for canvas edits. Positions and connections save with the project. On smaller screens, use the scene navigator and editing panels.'],tip:'You can navigate and rearrange the canvas without generating an image. Keep the main story path readable before adding alternative outcomes.'},
 {id:'scene',title:'Write a complete scene',time:'4 min',page:'scenes',action:'Edit scenes',intro:'A scene should describe a specific moment, with clear action and an emotional purpose.',steps:['Choose New Scene or Next Moment. Select existing characters and locations, or add the missing records first.','Write what happens, then add actions, emotions, dialogue, atmosphere, and camera direction. Describe how this moment changes the story.','Watch the live word count. A finalized scene needs at least 100 words; shorter scenes can stay as drafts.','Connect the scene to the previous moment, or create an alternative branch. Use the scene navigator to check the order, and preview the story to follow its choices.'],tip:'A character entering a library and discovering a hidden book are different story moments. Give each scene its own action and composition.'},
 {id:'director',title:'Prepare images and video',time:'4 min',page:'generation',action:'Open generation studio',intro:'Prepare prompts first, then explicitly choose whether to run a generation workflow.',steps:['Select your story and scene. In AI Scene Director, review the connected character references, location, and scene action.','Review and edit the text-to-image, image-to-video, and text-to-video prompts. Prompt preparation does not generate a paid image.','In Generation studio, choose a capability and available settings. Only the Generate action starts a job. The current mock workflow shows clearly labeled demonstration results.','Review job status and history, then save the result to the correct scene. For image-to-video, select the exact scene image as the starting reference. Preserve old versions and approve the one you want to use.'],tip:'Higgsfield live generation and payments remain disabled. Mock previews are demonstrations, not newly generated cinematic images or videos. Plans and credit estimates are preview functionality.'},
 {id:'finish',title:'Find gaps, save, and reopen',time:'3 min',page:'scenes',action:'Review story readiness',intro:'Use the readiness checks to bring a story from its opening through its ending.',steps:['Open the story readiness panel in Story workspace. Review missing descriptions, references, cast, locations, scene actions, and short drafts.','Complete the premise, beginning, conflict, climax, and resolution. Fill the specific missing details rather than generating unrelated assets.','Local changes save in this browser. Save a cloud snapshot when signed in to preserve linked records and reopen the project from Saved cloud projects.','Export the story and media backup for a portable copy. PDF imports retain source text and the original attachment on this device; download that original from the source panel.'],tip:'Browser storage is device-specific. Keep exports and original files as backups; do not assume local attachments are available on another device.'}
 ];
 let visible=$derived(lessons.filter(l=>(l.title+' '+l.intro+' '+l.steps.join(' ')).toLowerCase().includes(query.toLowerCase())));
 onMount(()=>{try{completed=JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem('eq-tutorial-progress')||'[]').filter(id=>lessons.some(l=>l.id===id));}catch{completed=[];}ready=true;});
 function toggle(id){completed=completed.includes(id)?completed.filter(x=>x!==id):[...completed,id];if(ready)try{localStorage.setItem('eq-tutorial-progress',JSON.stringify(completed));}catch{}}
</script>
<section class="tutorials">
 <div class="page-heading"><div><div class="eyebrow">THE ENCHANTED QUILL FIELD GUIDE</div><h1>A little guidance.<br/>A world of possibilities.</h1><p>Learn the workspace, build your story world, and bring every moment together.</p></div><BookOpen size={38}/></div>
 <div class="tutorial-progress surface"><div><strong>Your learning path</strong><span>{completed.length} of {lessons.length} lessons completed</span></div><progress value={completed.length} max={lessons.length} aria-label="Tutorial completion"></progress></div>
 <label class="tutorial-search"><Search size={18}/><input type="search" placeholder="Search tutorials, PDF, characters, canvas…" aria-label="Search tutorials" bind:value={query}/></label>
 <div class="tutorial-layout"><nav aria-label="Tutorial lessons">{#each visible as lesson,i}<button class:selected={active===lesson.id} onclick={()=>active=lesson.id}><span>{completed.includes(lesson.id)?'✓':String(lessons.indexOf(lesson)+1).padStart(2,'0')}</span><div><strong>{lesson.title}</strong><small>{lesson.time} read</small></div><ChevronDown size={14}/></button>{/each}</nav><div class="tutorial-lessons">{#each visible.filter(l=>l.id===active||query) as lesson}<article class="surface tutorial-lesson"><div class="eyebrow">LESSON {lessons.indexOf(lesson)+1} · {lesson.time}</div><h2>{lesson.title}</h2><p>{lesson.intro}</p><ol>{#each lesson.steps as step}<li>{step}</li>{/each}</ol><aside>{lesson.tip}</aside><div class="tutorial-actions"><button class="button primary" onclick={()=>onnavigate(lesson.page)}>{lesson.action}<ArrowRight size={16}/></button><button class="button secondary" aria-pressed={completed.includes(lesson.id)} onclick={()=>toggle(lesson.id)}>{#if completed.includes(lesson.id)}<Check size={16}/>{/if}{completed.includes(lesson.id)?'Completed':'Mark as complete'}</button></div>{#if lessons.indexOf(lesson)<lessons.length-1}<button class="text-button tutorial-next" onclick={()=>{active=lessons[lessons.indexOf(lesson)+1].id;query='';}}>Next: {lessons[lessons.indexOf(lesson)+1].title}<ArrowRight size={14}/></button>{/if}</article>{/each}{#if !visible.length}<div class="surface tutorial-lesson"><h2>No matching lessons</h2><p>Try “PDF”, “canvas”, “scene”, or “save”.</p><button class="button secondary" onclick={()=>query=''}>Show all lessons</button></div>{:else if !visible.some(l=>l.id===active)&&!query}<button class="button secondary" onclick={()=>active=visible[0].id}>Open first lesson</button>{/if}</div></div>
</section>
<style>
 .tutorials{max-width:1100px;margin:auto}.tutorials .page-heading{align-items:center}.tutorials h1{font-size:clamp(32px,3vw,48px);line-height:1.12}.tutorial-progress{padding:22px 26px;margin:12px 0 24px}.tutorial-progress div{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap}.tutorial-progress span{opacity:.65;font-size:14px}progress{width:100%;height:7px;accent-color:#d9f34a;margin-top:16px}.tutorial-search{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;border:1px solid #8884;border-radius:12px;padding:13px 17px;margin-bottom:28px}.tutorial-search input{background:transparent;border:0;color:inherit;font:inherit;width:100%;outline:0;min-width:0}.tutorial-search:focus-within{outline:2px solid #b4ca24}.tutorial-layout{display:grid;grid-template-columns:255px minmax(0,1fr);gap:28px}.tutorial-layout nav{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:7px;align-self:start;position:sticky;top:18px}.tutorial-layout nav button{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;text-align:left;padding:15px 12px;border:1px solid transparent;border-radius:12px;background:transparent;color:inherit;cursor:pointer}.tutorial-layout nav button:hover{background:#8881}.tutorial-layout nav button.selected{border-color:#b6ca2b;background:#b6ca2b12}.tutorial-layout nav button>span{font-size:13px;opacity:.6}.tutorial-layout nav strong{font-size:15px;display:block;line-height:1.4}.tutorial-layout nav small{display:block;font-size:12px;opacity:.55;margin-top:5px}.tutorial-layout nav :global(svg){margin-left:auto;flex-shrink:0}.tutorial-lessons{min-width:0;display:grid;gap:24px}.tutorial-lesson{padding:clamp(22px,3vw,38px);border-radius:18px}.tutorial-lesson h2{font-size:28px;line-height:1.25;margin:14px 0}.tutorial-lesson p,.tutorial-lesson li{font-size:16px;line-height:1.8}.tutorial-lesson p{opacity:.72}.tutorial-lesson ol{padding-left:24px;margin:24px 0}.tutorial-lesson li{padding-left:8px;margin:16px 0}.tutorial-lesson li::marker{color:#8c9c16;font-weight:700}.tutorial-lesson aside{padding:18px;border:1px solid #8884;border-radius:12px;font-size:14px;line-height:1.7}.tutorial-actions{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:12px;margin-top:26px}.tutorial-next{margin-top:24px;text-align:left;line-height:1.6}button:focus-visible{outline:2px solid #b6ca2b;outline-offset:3px}@media(max-width:850px){.tutorial-layout{grid-template-columns:1fr}.tutorial-layout nav{position:static;display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr))}.tutorial-layout nav button{min-width:0}.tutorials .page-heading>:global(svg){display:none}}@media(max-width:480px){.tutorial-layout nav{grid-template-columns:1fr}.tutorial-actions .button{width:100%;justify-content:center}.tutorial-lesson h2{font-size:25px}.tutorial-progress{padding:20px}}
</style>
